diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index d1d6b3d..266ef13 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -5,3 +5,7 @@ RAM-backed block device and sparse seed storage.
 used for the RAM-backed Data volume and the optional persistent overlay.
 
 Build and interface details: [documentation](https://unixnu.com/drivers/ram-block). Component sources and dependencies: [catalog](https://unixnu.com/reference/components).
+
+First zero-only writes to unallocated sparse pages keep them unallocated. A serialized 4KiB scratch buffer preserves partial/short-copy counts; nonzero writes allocate zero-filled pages. Write-through overlays still commit zero pages.
+
+Publishes standard solid-state medium characteristics for RAM and the optional UFS-backed store before storage-family startup. This lets the original kernel select its solid-state I/O periods; throttling policy is unchanged.
